  "body": "Buildable slice from the tracker data model investigation (#2029, PR #2281).\n\n**What:** a library-only module (`pkgs/id/src/didit/`) implementing the schema types and the pure evaluator from the investigation doc:\n\n- `Entity`, `Record` (subject set + per-subject `details` map + optional `measure`), `Expectation` (window as data, `supersedes`), `Opinion` (names its targets by event ID).\n- The four `didit.*` event kinds on `ChainExt.kind`, with CBOR bodies committed by the header payload hash.\n- `evaluate(events, now, tz) -> Vec<Verdict>` — pure, offline, replayable, no stored due state.\n- Summary and full projections for cross-app retrieval.\n\n**Why:** the schema is the blocker for the tracker half of the first ID app; it needs no runtime service and can land before the app exists.\n\n**Acceptance:**\n- [ ] Golden evaluation tests, including a DST transition in `America/Chicago` and a wrapping active span.\n- [ ] Every worked example from the investigation (fed twice daily, outside every 2–4h waking window, one-vs-both walk with divergent detail, water record, later opinion) round-trips: encode → sign → decode → identical bytes.\n- [ ] Supersede ordering asserted by causal position, not arrival order.\n- [ ] Summary projection drops exactly the named fields and keeps IDs stable, so an opinion still resolves.\n\nDesign doc: `doc/2026-10-29T13-04-50Z_investigation_didit_tracker_data_model/`. Open questions it leaves (clock authority for window boundaries, summary-projection leakage, retirement vs live expectations) are settled in that design round, not here.",
